Hi everyone.  This question has been asked before by others, but never  
with any answers, so I thought I'd try again :)  I'm having trouble  
getting XFree4 running on my UP2000(264dp).  It seems to switch to vt9  
and then it sits and takes 100% cpu until I ssh in and kill X.   
Afterward, I can switch back to whatever virtual terminal I want.  It  
appears to die after the pci bus scan.  XFree86 -scanpci works and  
exits properly.  I've tried several cards (S3 Virge and matrox) in  
several pci slots.  It behaves the same on all versions of X 4.1.0 to  
4.3.0, and all versions of FreeBSD 4.7 to -CURRENT from a couple nights  
ago.  XFree3.3.6 works however, but lacks lots of nice features

Here's my XFree86.0.log: (note, I disabled scanning the 2nd pci bus in  
the X source because I read on a debian-alpha mailing list that X had  
trouble scanning the 2nd bus on this board, but it didn't alter the  
behavior except that the 2nd bus is no longer scanned :)

Thanks for any advice you can give.

