From peter at larkowski.net  Sun Oct 12 11:29:42 2003
From: peter at larkowski.net (Peter Larkowski)
Date: Sun Oct 12 11:30:14 2003
Subject: XFree on a UP2000
In-Reply-To: <9E758D73-FAAB-11D7-BB60-003065707958@larkowski.net>
Message-ID: <0A012B9E-FCE2-11D7-A7A9-003065707958@larkowski.net>

Hi again, for those that have had this problem in the past, I thought a  
solution posted to the mailing list would be useful.  It was suggested  
to me that I should build XFree86 witht the int10 module disabled.  In  
trying to figure out how to do this, I stumbled across the changelog  
for the 4.3.99 (4.4.0) XFree86 pre releases and it seems there has been  
a problem with int10 on non-linux, non-x86 (ie, FreeBSD/alpha) that is  
now fixed.  I installed the XFree86-4-Server-snap port which is version  
4.3.99.12_2 right now (required disabling DRI on 5.X, seems to build  
fine on 4.X).  XFree86 -configure caused the on-board scsi to freak  
out, but once I gave it a config file, it works fine.

-p


